  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 159 AM CST Wed Nov 11 2026\n\nBy Sunday, longwave troughing is anticipated to begin departing the \neastern CONUS with cyclonic flow weakening over the Mid-Mississippi \nRiver Valley as heights rise. Global model guidance is coming into \nmuch better agreement that this process and the retreat of the \nsurface anticyclone will be slow, with NBM temperatures tightly \nclustered only a very gradual moderation in temperatures toward \naverage through early next week. At the same time, there remains a \nsignal for an upper-level trough to track from the Central Plains to \nthe Mid/Lower Mississippi River Valley Sunday into Monday. This \nfeature will likely at least provide increased clouds that help slow \nthe aforementioned warming trend, but global ensemble model \nprobabilities of any measurable rainfall only reach 20 to 30 percent \nacross central and southeastern MO with the highest probabilities \nacross KS, OK, and AR. Therefore, the prospects of rainfall are \nquestionable at this point.",
